@startuml SQL Server Internal Architecture

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

title SQL Server Internal Architecture – UPDATE Command Flow

actor "Client Application" as Client

rectangle "SQL Server" {

  rectangle "Protocol Layer" as Protocol {
    [Tabular Data\nStream (TDS)] as TDS
  }

  rectangle "Relational Engine" as Relational {
    [Parser]
    [Algebrizer]
    [Optimizer]
    [Query Executor]
  }

  rectangle "Storage Engine" as Storage {
    [Access Methods]
    [Buffer Manager]
    [Transaction Manager]
    [Lock Manager]
  }
}

database "Data Files" as MDF
database "Transaction Log" as LDF

' Flow
Client --> TDS : 1. TDS Packet\n(UPDATE Command)
TDS --> Parser : 2. Parse SQL
Parser --> Algebrizer : 3. Name Resolution
Algebrizer --> Optimizer : 4. Logical Plan
Optimizer --> [Query Executor] : 5. Execution Plan
[Query Executor] --> [Access Methods] : 6. Data Access
[Access Methods] --> [Buffer Manager] : 7. Page Retrieval
[Buffer Manager] --> MDF : 8. Disk Read/Write
[Access Methods] --> [Lock Manager] : 9. Acquire/Release Locks
[Access Methods] --> [Transaction Manager] : 10. Begin/Commit Transaction
[Transaction Manager] --> LDF : 11. Log Changes
[Query Executor] --> TDS : 12. Return Result
TDS --> Client : 13. Completion

legend right
  Key Components:
  - Protocol Layer: Handles communication (TDS)
  - Relational Engine: Parses, optimizes, and executes queries
  - Storage Engine: Manages data access, buffer, locks, and transactions
  - Data Files: Persistent storage (MDF)
  - Transaction Log: Ensures durability (LDF)
endlegend

@enduml
